  "reason": "Evidence: config_041 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.520) and F1 (0.479) so far, but with only one data point the evidence is sparse. The key uncertainty is whether weighted fusion is optimal or whether concat fusion could yield better accuracy with the same strong encoders and transformer aggregation. This experiment (config_002) changes only the fusion type from weighted to concat, making it a clean single-variable test that directly exploits the most promising architecture while reducing uncertainty about the fusion mechanism. It is the best use of experiment 2 because it builds on the strongest signal we have, is a minimal-risk exploitation step, and will cost approximately the same ~2.8–3.0 GPU hours as config_041 (same multiprofile transformer aggregation with scgpt and imagenet_vit_l encoders), keeping total compute low while gathering critical information to guide the remaining 8 experiments."
}

